       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nCould the intended dose be one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1000 mg.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale for the order note."
